//! HTTP tracker protocol implementation.
//!
//! This module handles communication with BitTorrent trackers. Trackers are
//! servers that help peers discover each other. The client announces itself
//! to the tracker and receives a list of peers sharing the same torrent.
//!
//! # Protocol Overview
//!
//! 1. Client sends HTTP GET request to tracker's announce URL with parameters:
//!    - `info_hash`: 20-byte torrent identifier
//!    - `peer_id`: 20-byte client identifier
//!    - `port`: port client is listening on
//!    - `uploaded`, `downloaded`, `left`: transfer statistics
//!    - `event`: started, stopped, or completed (optional)
//!
//! 2. Tracker responds with bencoded dictionary containing:
//!    - `interval`: seconds until next announce
//!    - `peers`: list of peers (compact or dictionary format)
//!    - Optionally: `tracker id`, `complete`, `incomplete`
//!
//! # Error Handling
//!
//! Tracker communication can fail in several ways. The [`TrackerError`] enum
//! provides detailed error information to enable appropriate recovery strategies.

